yamlover/tag
description: The !!<…> inline schema tag — metadata riding the value
- >
  The `!!<…>` tag carries a value's METADATA inline, and its contents are themselves yamlover —
  either a pointer to a hosted schema (`!!<*yamlover: $defs: chapter>`) or an inline literal
  (`!!<format: text/x-plantuml>`). It is the file-concrete counterpart of a directory's
  `.yo/meta.yo`, and yamlover-only — json5p has no tags. YAML's `!tag` is the kin, one name
  where yamlover carries a whole schema — the subclass:
- !!<format: text/x-yamlover> |
  diagram: !!<format: text/x-plantuml> |
    @startuml
    A -> B
    @enduml
- *..:..:..:..:..:..:01-yaml:01-yaml_code:00-yaml_structured:00-yaml_mapping:02-yaml_key_value_pair:02-yaml_tag
